Umm.

Actually, the "[letter]lock.[number]" files are the level insurance files.

The synopsis on the recover man page states "recover [ -d directory ] base1
base2 ...".

Blair has two lock sets on his box, "a" and "c": "alock" and "clock" are the
bases.  Since recover is usually installed in the NETHACKDIR, to recover "a",
for example, he would run "./recover -d . alock".

As his later post says he successfully "fg"d the game, this is unnecessary, but
I figured you both might like to know this for future reference.  ;-)

(6 years of running the tournament have _definitely_ taught me how to use
recover ... )

